; The counting loop of the division variant of the Nexus M1 fixture. It is the
; loop of the fixture with a test that divides by the counter: the remainder of
; a number larger than any counter is never the number less one, so the loop
; runs the counter down to zero, where the division has a zero divisor and the
; run ends in `@runtime.division-by-zero`, which has no origin. `finish` is
; never called.
(defn count (finish (fn () str) remaining u64) str
  visibility: @public
  (if
    (equatable.equal (u64.rem 1000000u64 remaining) 999999u64)
    (finish)
    (count finish (u64.sub remaining 1u64))))
